+++ b/crates/cua-macos-visual/PROVENANCE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,191 @@
+# cua-macos-visual provenance
+
+Fixed upstream revision: `2d2f99228d4d2508dc6fcc84c176b296e146714a`
+
+Fixed upstream source root: `libs/cua-driver/rust`
+
+This crate is a functional subset, not an ABI-equivalent replacement for the
+R7 SDK graph. It owns one observation's window facts, pixels and conversion
+checks only. It does not own submissions, leases, frame publication, input
+dispatch, AX semantics, screen recording, clipboard, overlay/PiP, browser or
+daemon lifecycle.
+
+## Source mapping
+
+### `crates/platform-macos/src/windows.rs` -> `src/window.rs`
+
+Kept:
+
+- `CGWindowListCopyWindowInfo` restricted to on-screen, non-desktop-element
+  windows (`kCGWindowListOptionOnScreenOnly |
+  kCGWindowListExcludeDesktopElements`).
+- Optional reads of `kCGWindowNumber`, `kCGWindowOwnerPID`, `kCGWindowLayer`
+  and all four `kCGWindowBounds` components.
+- Pure checked parsing (`RawWindowFact` -> `WindowIdentity`): missing keys,
+  non-finite values, non-positive sizes, non-layer-0 windows and values that do
+  not fit `u32`/`i32` are rejected. Nothing is defaulted to `0` or truncated.
+
+Removed:
+
+- `kCGWindowOwnerName`, `kCGWindowName`, z-index, on-screen and Space fields.
+- SkyLight Space queries, AX reachability filtering and helper-window pruning.
+- All public window enumeration and selection helpers. The remaining reader is
+  `pub(crate)` and only reachable from the crate-private capture path.
+
+Not supported this round: off-Space, minimized and accessory/overlay windows.
+Because enumeration is on-screen only, an absent window is `WindowNotFound`, not
+a silently accepted zero fact. A request with a non-zero layer is rejected.
+
+### R8 `crates/platform-macos/src/capture.rs` -> R9 `src/capture.rs` + `src/observe.rs` + `native/CuaVisualCapture.swift`
+
+R8 depended on the general `screencapturekit` Rust wrapper. R9 removes that
+wrapper from this crate and derives a narrow Swift completion bridge from the
+fixed wrapper's Swift sources; the exact archive, source hashes, licenses and
+delta are recorded in [`native/DERIVATION.md`](native/DERIVATION.md).
+
+Kept semantically in the Swift bridge:
+
+- `SCShareableContent` on-screen enumeration and exact `windowID` selection.
+- `SCContentFilter(desktopIndependentWindow:)`, `pointPixelScale`/`contentRect`
+  sizing and `SCStreamConfiguration.showsCursor = false`, now with an explicit
+  `kCVPixelFormatType_32BGRA` pixel format.
+- `SCScreenshotManager.captureImage` and a bounded `CGImage` to RGBA conversion.
+- Identity revalidation before capture, against the selected SCK window and
+  after the frame returns. Drift is rejected; the window is never reselected.
+
+Changed for R9:
+
+- The bridge uses the framework completion handler instead of the wrapper's
+  `Task`/`SyncCompletion`, and passes no Rust userdata pointer.
+- `LifecycleGate` makes enumeration, admission, capture and terminal delivery
+  once-only, so a duplicate framework callback cannot enter admission or end an
+  operation whose first capture is still in flight.
+- RGBA byte and pixel budgets are checked before `SCScreenshotManager` is
+  called, not only while rendering.
+- `payloadReleased` is an explicit `@convention(c) (UInt64) -> Void` callback
+  sent after the bridge-owned pixel buffer is deallocated. It releases in-flight
+  capacity; it does not claim OS callback-thread exit or native `Fenced`/`Drained`.
+
+Added Rust ownership:
+
+- `src/session.rs` owns one bounded observation registry (four slots),
+  monotonic result-reception cancellation, a cloneable cancel handle, one-shot
+  `wait` (`CaptureAlreadyConsumed` on a second call) and idempotent
+  completion/release. Observer `Drop` also closes reception.
+- `src/observe.rs` keeps the injected before/select/capture/after/encode order
+  and adds a final cancellation check after PNG verification. That check is the
+  result-delivery linearization point, not an OS callback exit.
+
+Removed:
+
+- `screencapturekit`, `apple-metal`, `apple-cf`, stream recording, audio,
+  content-sharing picker, Metal texture bridge, cache/timeout/retry and the
+  shell/SkyLight fallbacks.
+
+Not solved here:
+
+- Cancelling result reception is not native stop. A capture already admitted in
+  Swift may still start and its late result is dropped; a missing native
+  callback keeps the slot and the wait pending because no timeout is added.
+- `payloadReleased` is not a native `Fenced`/`Drained` signal and does not prove
+  that the OS callback thread has returned.
+- CGWindow identity agreement is observation consistency only. It is not
+  process-incarnation proof, authorization, a lease or a published final frame.
+
+### `crates/cua-driver-core/src/image_utils.rs` -> `src/png.rs`
+
+Kept:
+
+- `encode_rgba_to_png`, now using `PngEncoder` directly from the caller's slice
+  with no `rgba.to_vec()` clone.
+- `png_dimensions` as an explicitly header-only IHDR parser.
+
+Added:
+
+- `verify_png_matches_dimensions` first bounds the input length and walks the
+  chunk container with checked lengths. It verifies every chunk CRC, requires
+  IHDR first, at least one IDAT and a final zero-length IEND, and rejects any
+  trailing bytes. `image` then performs only the bounded pixel decode. This
+  rejects a 24-byte IHDR-only fake, truncation (including a missing IEND), a bad
+  IEND or other chunk CRC, trailing garbage, non-RGBA8 colour type, wrong pixel
+  byte count and aggregate pixel/RGBA budget overflow before a success frame can
+  be formed.
+- Aggregate pixel/RGBA budget checks (`MAX_CAPTURE_PIXELS`, `MAX_RGBA_BYTES`)
+  in addition to the per-side limit.
+
+Removed:
+
+- JPEG encoding, PNG-to-JPEG conversion, resizing, crosshair drawing and
+  BGRA conversion.
+- The workspace `image` feature set. This crate depends on `image 0.25` with
+  `default-features = false, features = ["png"]`, so JPEG encoding is not
+  compiled through this crate's direct dependency.
+
+### `crates/platform-macos/src/tools/px_frame.rs` -> `src/geometry.rs`
+
+Kept:
+
+- `validate_capture_frame`'s coherent 1x/2x scale rule and refusal on zero or
+  non-finite bounds.
+
+Removed:
+
+- `WindowPxFrame::to_screen`. It has no validated caller in this round, and an
+  unchecked public pixel-to-screen transform would accept NaN/infinity or a
+  zero scale. It is not carried as a public API.
+- `ToolResult` refusal JSON, `error_structured`, `resolve_or_refuse` and the
+  native `resolve_window_px_frame` convenience. This crate exposes only pure
+  geometry; a frame is not wired to action dispatch.
+
+## Dependency and platform notes
+
+- This crate's native closure is `core-foundation` plus the derived
+  `native/CuaVisualCapture.swift` bridge. It no longer depends on the general
+  `screencapturekit`, `apple-metal` or `apple-cf` wrapper. Those package entries
+  remain in the workspace lock because the old SDK/platform roots still use
+  them; this crate does not, and the probe graph confirms their absence here.
+- `build.rs` selects the compiler and SDK only through the absolute
+  `/usr/bin/xcrun`: `--find swiftc` and `--sdk macosx27.0 --show-sdk-path`. It
+  verifies one absolute `<toolchain>/usr/bin/swiftc`, the installed SDK
+  directory, and the SDK's real Swift autolink stub
+  (`<SDK>/usr/lib/swift/libswiftCore.tbd`). Missing compiler/SDK/stub,
+  unsupported architecture or compile failure aborts; there is no SDK fallback.
+- The bridge is compiled with `-parse-as-library -emit-object -swift-version 5
+  -O -target arm64-apple-macos14.2 -sdk <SDK>` through the CLT Swift 6.4
+  driver, then archived with `/usr/bin/libtool`.
+- `build.rs` adds `<SDK>/usr/lib/swift` as a native link search path, emits
+  `cargo:rustc-link-arg=-Wl,-syslibroot,<SDK>` and
+  `cargo:rustc-link-arg=-Wl,-rpath,/usr/lib/swift` for this crate's test/final
+  executable. The independent probe crate adds the same syslibroot/rpath
+  itself; an rlib does not carry either. No `DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH`, copied system
+  library, disabled validation, ignored symbol, docs.rs bypass or global SDK
+  change is used.
+- The Swift object's real `LC_LINKER_OPTION` entries include ScreenCaptureKit,
+  Foundation, CoreFoundation and Metal frameworks plus system Swift overlays
+  (`swiftCore`, `swift_Concurrency`, `swiftMetal`, `swiftAVFoundation`,
+  `swiftCoreAudio`, `swiftCoreImage`, `swiftCoreMIDI`, `swiftIOKit`,
+  `swiftQuartzCore`, `swiftSpatial`, `swiftXPC`, `swiftos`, `swiftsimd`, ...).
+  It carries no `libswiftCompatibility56`/`libswiftCompatibilityPacks`
+  force-load, so those archives are not a prerequisite.
+- The object and the independent consumer both record `minos 14.2` and
+  `sdk 27.0`; the consumer records `LC_RPATH=/usr/lib/swift`. An earlier local
+  `macosx15.2` pin was a non-reproducible misdiagnosis and is not used.
+- No cache, lease, registry migration, shell, SkyLight, AX SPI or TCC request is
+  introduced.
+
+## License
+
+- `LICENSE-MIT` is a verbatim copy of the fixed upstream root `LICENSE.md` at
+  `2d2f99228d4d2508dc6fcc84c176b296e146714a`, SHA-256
+  `c0779290c1d4783169aa3dbfb55feb505e563ef8a004bbf55298ceffcfbda8d9`,
+  1069 bytes. It is not a template.
+- The crate expression is the workspace `MIT`; the copied text is the actual
+  copyright/license body from the fixed upstream object. The CUA root MIT text
+  does not cover the derived ScreenCaptureKit material.
+- The derived bridge retains the upstream dual-license texts verbatim under
+  `native/licenses/`: `LICENSE-MIT` (1091 bytes, SHA-256
+  `5464a5ed6a2143a9d31e5516c7336a312c3c067cdc6ad15323f18fdf8d9755ae`) and
+  `LICENSE-APACHE` (11358 bytes, SHA-256
+  `cfc7749b96f63bd31c3c42b5c471bf756814053e847c10f3eb003417bc523d30`). See
+  `native/DERIVATION.md` for the archive checksum, git revision and per-file
+  digests.
